window.soraCatalogue = {"property":{"name":"Sora House","tagline":"A slower way to stay.","location":"Atlantic coast, Portugal","coordinates":"38.7° N · 9.5° W","roomsTotal":12,"currency":"EUR","timezone":"Europe/Lisbon","minStayNights":1,"maxStayNights":14},"rooms":[{"name":"Dune Room","slug":"dune","category":"Room","units":4,"areaSqm":26,"maxGuests":2,"rate":180,"view":"Garden","short":"Our smallest rooms, tucked behind the dunes and facing the garden.","description":"The Dune Room sits at the back of the house, where the land rises into the dune grass. It is a small, calm room with one deep window, a low bed and a bench that fits two people and a book. In the morning the light comes in sideways and the garden is the first thing you see.","story":"We designed these four rooms for the people who came to Sora House to do nothing in particular. There is a chair, a table, a shelf of books that guests have left behind, and a deep sill to sit on. The plaster is warm to the touch by ten in the morning. From the bed you can hear the sea, but only just — which is the point.","features":["Deep window with a stone sill","King or twin beds","Reading lamps and a small writing desk","Walk-in shower with lime-washed walls","Private patio onto the dune garden"],"amenities":["Breakfast included","House car for local transfers","Beach towels and robes","Daily water and fruit","Folded map of the coast"],"gallery":[{"file":"../../assets/rooms/dune-room-main.svg","alt":"The Dune Room with an arched window opening onto the dune garden."},{"file":"../../assets/rooms/dune-room-02.svg","alt":"The Dune Room in daylight, with a low bed and a bench under the window."},{"file":"../../assets/rooms/dune-room-03.svg","alt":"Linen bedding folded on the Dune Room bed."}],"related":["courtyard","atlantic"]},{"name":"Courtyard Room","slug":"courtyard","category":"Room","units":3,"areaSqm":32,"maxGuests":2,"rate":230,"view":"Courtyard","short":"Three rooms around a sheltered courtyard of stone, olive and shade.","description":"The Courtyard Rooms open onto the planted heart of the house. They are larger than the Dune Rooms and lit from above rather than from the side, which makes them cool in the middle of the day and warm in the evening.","story":"The courtyard was the first thing we built. It is a square of local stone with three olives, a bench and a shallow water rill that runs in winter. Around it, the three Courtyard Rooms each have a wide window onto it. Guests often take breakfast here, though we will always bring it to your door if you would rather stay put.","features":["Wide window onto the courtyard","King or twin beds","Deep stone bath or walk-in shower","Reading chair and floor lamp","Separate shelf and wardrobe"],"amenities":["Breakfast included","House car for local transfers","Beach towels and robes","Daily water and fruit","Courtyard breakfast table"],"gallery":[{"file":"../../assets/rooms/courtyard-room-main.svg","alt":"The Courtyard Room with an arched opening onto the planted courtyard."},{"file":"../../assets/rooms/courtyard-room-02.svg","alt":"The Courtyard Room in daylight, with a wide window over the courtyard."},{"file":"../../assets/rooms/courtyard-room-03.svg","alt":"Afternoon light moving across the plaster wall of a Courtyard Room."}],"related":["dune","suite"]},{"name":"Atlantic Room","slug":"atlantic","category":"Room","units":4,"areaSqm":38,"maxGuests":2,"rate":310,"view":"Atlantic","short":"A wide west-facing window, a deep terrace, and the horizon at eye level.","description":"The Atlantic Rooms are the widest of the four categories and face west across open sand. Each has a terrace deep enough to eat on, a window that runs almost the length of the wall, and the particular quality of light you only get an hour before sunset.","story":"We kept these rooms deliberately plain so that the view does the work. The walls are unpainted lime plaster. The floor is wide oak boards with a rug woven in a village twenty kilometres inland. The terrace has two chairs and nothing else, because at this hour you will want to be facing the water. At night the curtains are heavy and the sea disappears behind them.","features":["Private terrace with two chairs","Full-width west-facing window","King or twin beds","Stone bath with an ocean window","Writing desk facing the sea"],"amenities":["Breakfast included","House car for local transfers","Beach towels and robes","Daily water and fruit","Evening aperitif on the terrace"],"gallery":[{"file":"../../assets/rooms/atlantic-room-main.svg","alt":"The Atlantic Room: a wide window framing the sea, a low bed and a private terrace beyond."},{"file":"../../assets/rooms/atlantic-room-02.svg","alt":"The Atlantic Room in the late afternoon, with the terrace door open to the west."},{"file":"../../assets/rooms/atlantic-room-03.svg","alt":"The coast seen from the Atlantic Room terrace."}],"related":["courtyard","suite"]},{"name":"Sora Suite","slug":"suite","category":"Suite","units":1,"areaSqm":54,"maxGuests":3,"rate":430,"view":"Atlantic","short":"Our only suite, with a separate lounge and the widest outlook on the coast.","description":"The Sora Suite occupies the western end of the house. It has a bedroom, a separate lounge with its own fireplace, and a wide view of the Atlantic.","story":"We built one suite rather than two because the plan only works once. The lounge has a low fire for the evenings when the wind turns, and a long sofa that sleeps one if you need it. In the morning the suite is quiet enough to hear the water arrive on the sand, which takes about twenty minutes and is worth staying in bed for.","features":["Separate lounge with a fireplace","Private terrace with a day bed","King bed plus a sofa bed","Freestanding stone bath","Dressing room and two wardrobes"],"amenities":["Breakfast included","House car for local transfers","Beach towels and robes","Daily water and fruit","Private dinner in the suite"],"gallery":[{"file":"../../assets/rooms/sora-suite-main.svg","alt":"The Sora Suite bedroom with an arched opening towards the sea."},{"file":"../../assets/rooms/sora-suite-02.svg","alt":"The Sora Suite lounge, with a long sofa and an arched window facing west."},{"file":"../../assets/rooms/sora-suite-03.svg","alt":"Oak boards in the Sora Suite."}],"related":["atlantic","courtyard"]}]};
